2019 was a low yield due to heat during flowering and 3 major frosts at Barossa Valley. The bottle was one of the random Australian picks to complete my wine order. Turned out to be a good surprise with very intriguing nose and smooth finishing. Rather young. 

👁 Deep purple; 
👃 Damp, musty, black fruit, mushroom, milk chocolate, forest floor;
👅 Plum, pepper, mildly chalky, burnt marshmallow, smooth finish.

Light red without note;
Young and quite uninspired;
No need to try this.
